    },
    {
      "id": "WSSvL6xJI5teVDBF3gQDW",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 415.698062116971,
      "y": 1154.2995402400868,
      "width": 529.3275146484375,
      "height": 320,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ad",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1437998033,
      "version": 1646,
      "versionNonce": 2112917279,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1777333701054,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Create two variables for prt1 and ptr2 -> O(1) space complexity\n2. Convert the string to an array\n3. Set ptr1 to 0 and ptr2 to string array count - 1\n4. While ptr1 is less than ptr2 -> O(n) time complexity\n    5. If string array subscript ptr1 is a non alphanumeric character\n        6. Set ptr1 to ptr1 + 1 to skip the character\n        7. Go to the line 4\n    8. If string array subscript ptr2 is a non alphanumeric character\n        9. Set ptr2 to ptr2 - 1 to skip the character\n        10. Go to the line 4\n    11. If ptr1 and ptr2 are equal\n        12. Set ptr1 to ptr1 + 1\n        13. Set ptr2 to ptr2 - 1\n        14. Go to the line 4\n    15. Else\n16. Return true",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Create two variables for prt1 and ptr2 -> O(1) space complexity\n2. Convert the string to an array\n3. Set ptr1 to 0 and ptr2 to string array count - 1\n4. While ptr1 is less than ptr2 -> O(n) time complexity\n    5. If string array subscript ptr1 is a non alphanumeric character\n        6. Set ptr1 to ptr1 + 1 to skip the character\n        7. Go to the line 4\n    8. If string array subscript ptr2 is a non alphanumeric character\n        9. Set ptr2 to ptr2 - 1 to skip the character\n        10. Go to the line 4\n    11. If ptr1 and ptr2 are equal\n        12. Set ptr1 to ptr1 + 1\n        13. Set ptr2 to ptr2 - 1\n        14. Go to the line 4\n    15. Else\n16. Return true",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
